  "output" : "I've read the context file and explored the implementation (`graph.html`, `graph.js`, `GraphHandler.swift`, `GraphStore.swift`). Your description matches the code — here's the mental model confirmed against the actual mechanics, with a few nuances worth having pinned down:\n\n## The tree (knowledge flow)\n- Nodes live in SQLite (`graph_nodes` per instance) as `parent_id`-linked rows; the UI renders them as depth columns of cells (`buildColumns()`), with bird's-eye lanes per root→leaf chain.\n- Each cell carries: prompt, agent, per-node remote MCP (url + auth header), optional personas, a name, and an `active` flag. Editing a node happens in the right detail panel (name/mcp/summary/personas/active/delete).\n\n## Run = pickup from a node's point in time\n- `POST /graph/:nid/run` → `runLogFor(...)` builds the ancestor chain via `GraphStore.chain(of:in:)` and **requires every ancestor to be `success`** (i.e. answered *and* summarized) — otherwise the Run button is disabled (\"chain not ready — parents need summaries\").\n- The \"prior knowledge\" the agent receives is **the chain's summaries**, not raw outputs: joined with `---` into `ctx.md`, placed in a per-run temp dir and injected as a \"Context file: /context/ctx.md — read it before answering\" prompt prefix (that's the same pattern as the ctx.md you had me read). Chain MCP endpoints are also merged into a generated MCP config, and personas run with the `_bottom_` persona.\n- Lifecycle: `progress` → `summarizing` (auto Q&A summary) → `success` (summary stored) / `answered` (no summary) / `failed`. Inactive ancestors are skipped from the chain entirely.\n\n## Follow-ups on a focused run\n- Focusing a run (→ arrow / \"Conversation\" view) shows the thread (`root_run_id` groups it; \"+N\" badge in the runs list).\n- A follow-up posts `parent_run_id` = the **tip** run, and must satisfy: tip is `success` (has a summary — composer only renders then) and has no children (\"append to the conversation tip\"). Backend writes `convo.md` (joined run-chain summaries) alongside the node-chain `ctx.md`, both prefixed into the prompt. Failed tips get Retry instead of a composer.\n\nOther invariants I noted: 5s polling refresh, insert-before reparenting, delete-node bridges children up while delete-chain removes the subtree (armed 2-step confirm, blocked while running), and interrupted runs get swept to `failed`/`answered` on next list.\n\nWhat would you like to do from here — a change/feature on graph.html, a bug, or something else?\n"
}
